---


<Layout

title="How To Play Wordle: Complete Beginner Guide"

description="Learn how to play Wordle with simple rules, strategies, and beginner tips."

>


<SEO

title="How To Play Wordle: Complete Beginner Guide"

description="Learn Wordle rules, gameplay instructions, and beginner strategies to solve daily puzzles."

canonical="/blog/how-to-play-wordle"

/>



<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />




<main class="article">


<header>


<h1>
How To Play Wordle: Complete Beginner Guide
</h1>


<p class="intro">

Learn the rules of Wordle, how guesses work, and simple strategies to solve the daily puzzle.

</p>


</header>





<section>


<h2>
What Is Wordle?
</h2>


<p>

Wordle is a daily five-letter word puzzle where players try to discover one hidden word within six attempts.

Each guess provides clues using colored tiles that show whether letters are correct, misplaced, or not included in the answer.

</p>


</section>





<section>


<h2>
How Does Wordle Work?
</h2>


<p>

Every day, Wordle gives players a new five-letter word challenge.

You enter a word, submit your guess, and receive feedback.

The goal is to identify the correct word using these clues.

</p>


</section>





<section>


<h2>
Understanding Wordle Colors
</h2>



<div class="tiles">


<div>

<span class="green">
A
</span>

<p>
Correct letter and correct position.
</p>

</div>



<div>

<span class="yellow">
B
</span>

<p>
Correct letter but wrong position.
</p>

</div>




<div>

<span class="gray">
C
</span>

<p>
Letter does not appear in the answer.
</p>

</div>



</div>


</section>





<section>


<h2>
Wordle Rules
</h2>


<ul>

<li>
You have six attempts to solve the puzzle.
</li>

<li>
Your answer must contain five letters.
</li>

<li>
Letters can repeat in some answers.
</li>

<li>
Each guess gives clues for the next attempt.
</li>

</ul>


</section>





<section>


<h2>
Beginner Wordle Tips
</h2>


<h3>
1. Start With Strong Opening Words
</h3>


<p>

Use words containing common vowels and frequently used letters.

Examples include words with letters like A, E, R, S, T, and L.

</p>




<h3>
2. Use The Feedback Carefully
</h3>


<p>

Green letters should remain in the same position.

Yellow letters should move to different positions.

Gray letters should usually be avoided.

</p>




<h3>
3. Avoid Random Guessing
</h3>


<p>

Use each attempt to collect information instead of simply trying random words.

</p>


</section>





<section>


<h2>
Need Help With Today's Puzzle?
</h2>


<p>

If you are stuck, you can use our progressive hints instead of revealing the answer immediately.

</p>


<a href="/today-wordle-hint">
Get Today's Wordle Hint →
</a>


</section>





<section>


<h2>
Want More Wordle Tools?
</h2>


<p>

You can also use our Wordle solver to find possible words based on your guesses.

</p>


<a href="/wordle-solver">
Try Wordle Solver →
</a>


</section>




<FAQ />


</main>



</Layout>




